{"at": "2026-09-24 23:20:45", "kind": "phase", "name": "memory", "payload": {"grounding": [{"id": "sar_guidance_narrative#p25-example-2", "section": "Example #2", "text": "Any further transactions sent by this sender will be kept on file. We will not be sending a report for every transaction. Thank you. Comments: The narrative only provides a reference to an unknown subject -\u201cthis sender,\u201d-- and fails to identify a possible violation. It gives no information on the amounts of the money transmittals or the beneficiary of the funds. The only value the narrative provides is to alert the reader that the MSB may be violating BSA regulations by not filing future SARs on"}, {"id": "policy#R6", "section": "3. Rules - R6. Shared origin.", "text": "Fraud Policy v1.0 (HHGOA dataset README). Rule R6: Shared origin. When several cards show fraud from the same device profile, the same billing region, or the same recipient email in one window, name the shared element, recommend `CREATE_CASE` and `FILE_REPORT`, and `MONITOR_CONNECTED_CARDS` for every card that shares it."}, {"id": "ffiec_sar_overview#p01-sar-filing-on-continuing-2", "section": "SAR Filing on Continuing Activity", "text": "Criteria for when analysis of the overall customer relationship is necessary. Criteria for whether and, if so, when to close the account. Criteria for when to notify law enforcement, if appropriate. ## SAR Completion and Filing SAR completion and filing are a critical part of the SAR monitoring and reporting process. Appropriate policies, procedures, and processes should be in place to ensure SARs are filed in a timely manner, are complete and accurate, and that the narrative provides a sufficie"}, {"id": "fatf_cyber_fraud_2023#p26-31-new-technologies-have", "section": "31.     New technologies have provided new benefits and opportunities for consumers.", "text": "There is a profound shift towards digitalisation of financial services, which accelerated during the COVID-19 pandemic. The r